/-!
# Étale coordinates adapted to a smooth flag

Let `X` be smooth over a field `k` and `Z ⊆ W ⊆ X` closed subschemes smooth over `k`, `p ∈ Z`,
and let `r`, `s` be the codimensions at `p` of `Z` and of `W` in `X`. Then there are an affine open
`U ∋ p` and local coordinates `x_1, …, x_n` on `U` (an étale `(x_1, …, x_n) : U ⟶ 𝔸^n_k`) with
`W ∩ U = V(x_1, …, x_s)` and `Z ∩ U = V(x_1, …, x_r)` as closed subschemes of `U`. In
particular a smooth closed subscheme is locally the pullback of a coordinate subspace under an
étale map to `𝔸^n_k`, `n = rank_p Ω_{X/k}`.

## Main results

* `MMP.Resolution.Bridges.exists_isLocalCoordinates_adapted_flag`: coordinates adapted to a
  smooth flag.
* `MMP.Resolution.Bridges.exists_isLocalCoordinates_isCutOutByFirst_of_stalk`: the same, from
  hypotheses at the stalk of the point only (regular, formally smooth quotients).
* `MMP.Resolution.Bridges.exists_isLocalCoordinates_adapted`: a smooth closed subscheme is
  locally `g⁻¹(V(x_1, …, x_c))` for an étale `g : U ⟶ 𝔸^n_k`, `n = rank_p Ω_{X/k}`.
* `MMP.Resolution.Bridges.exists_isLocalCoordinatesAt_adapted`: at a closed point, in
  characteristic zero, adapted differential coordinates all vanishing at the point, whose last
  `n - r` restrict to local coordinates on `Z`.

## Implementation notes

* Closed subschemes are ideal sheaves `Z : X.IdealSheafData`; `Z ⊆ W` is `W ≤ Z` (inclusion of
  ideal sheaves), and "`Z` smooth over `k`" is `Smooth (Z.subschemeι ≫ f)`. A point of `Z` is a
  point `z` of the subscheme, with image `Z.subschemeι z` in `X`.
* In the closed-point statement, local coordinates at `p` are
  `MMP.Resolution.IsLocalCoordinatesAt` (Kollár Def. 3.73: `dx_i` a basis of `Ω_{U/k}`, all `x_i`
  vanishing at `p`), the dimension `dim_p X` is `topologicalKrullDimAt`, and the restriction of a
  section of `𝒪_X(U)` to `Z ∩ U` is `Z.subschemeι.app U`.
* Étale local coordinates are `MMP.Resolution.IsLocalCoordinates` (Kollár (3.60.2)). The
  equality `Z ∩ U = V(x_1, …, x_r)` of closed subschemes of `U` is: on every affine open
  `V ⊆ U`, the ideal `I_Z(V)` is generated by the restrictions of `x_1, …, x_r`.
* The codimension at `p` of a closed subscheme `Z ⊆ X` is `dim_p X - dim_p Z`, with
  `dim_p = topologicalKrullDimAt` the dimension of small neighbourhoods; it is stated additively,
  `dim_p X = dim_p Z + r`.
* `rank_p Ω_{X/k}` is the rank of the stalk `Ω[𝒪_{X,p} ⁄ 𝒪_{Spec k, f p}]`, as in
  `MMP.Flips.ResolutionInputs.exists_isAffineOpen_etale_affineSpace`.
-/

@[expose] public section

